  "does_not_cover": "16.2(b) reads the four mediator crates the binary links, and nothing else. The crates they depend on read the environment too (logging, TLS roots, proxies, the Redis and AWS clients). Those reads are closed by the entrypoint's `env -i` with the allow list, and proven by the 16.2(c) /proc/<pid>/environ test, not by this grep. A green 16.2(b) means only: every name these four crates read was read by Security at this pin."
